{"seq":19,"slug":"decision-theory-philosophy","title":"决策论","stage":"DONE","category":"philosophy-logic","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy","rating":{"composite":3.96,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"决策论-在不确定中如何理性选择\">决策论：在不确定中如何理性选择</h1><p>一个人站在两份工作、两种疗法、两条投资路径之间，信息不全、后果难料，却仍必须选一个。决策论就是把这种「在不确定下做选择」的处境拆开来看的学问：它问的不是「你偏好什么」，而是「给定你的偏好与信念，怎样的选择才配得上『理性』二字」。它既是哲学的一支（关于理性本身的规范理论），又是经济学、统计学、人工智能共享的技术工具。</p>\n<p>这个 hub 沿四条主线递进，每一条都建立在前一条之上。第一条是<strong>基础</strong>：先讲清决策论要解决什么问题、它与心理学式的「人实际怎么选」有何根本区别，再搭起「状态—行动—结果」这套贯穿全书的形式骨架。第二条是<strong>效用</strong>，也是全书的技术核心：从期望效用原理出发，看冯·诺依曼与摩根斯坦如何用四条公理证明「凡偏好满足公理者，其行为必等价于最大化某个效用函数的期望」，再把这套框架落到风险态度上。第三条是<strong>争论</strong>：当决策涉及「我的选择本身会透露或影响什么」时，因果决策论与证据决策论分道扬镳，Newcomb 问题把这道裂缝撑到最大；而当概率本身都无法给定时，奈特不确定性与模糊登场。第四条是<strong>应用</strong>：Allais 与 Ellsberg 两个悖论如何证伪了标准理论，有限理性与前景理论如何描述真实的人，以及这套两百年的理论在医疗、政策、强化学习与 AI 对齐中如何落地又在何处失效。</p>\n<p>读法上给三种建议。只想建立直觉的读者，读完「基础」三篇即可对整个领域有骨架式的把握。想吃透规范理论的读者，重点在「效用」章的公理与表示定理，那是理解后续所有争论与悖论的钥匙。关心 AI 与现实决策的读者，可在读完基础后直接跳到「应用」章，再回头补「争论」章的因果/证据之别——现代 AI 决策理论正诞生于这道裂缝。</p>\n<p>与兄弟 hub 的分工要说清。本 hub 只讲<strong>单人</strong>在不确定下的理性选择；一旦对手是另一个会算计你的理性主体，那属于<a href=\"../../mathematics-statistics/game-theory/\">博弈论</a>与<a href=\"../../economics-finance/game-theory/\">经济学中的博弈论</a>。作为信念度量的概率演算不在此展开，见<a href=\"../../mathematics-statistics/probability-statistics/probability-foundations/bayes-theorem\">概率统计</a>与<a href=\"../epistemology/scientific-epistemology/bayesian-epistemology\">贝叶斯认识论</a>。「后果的好坏由什么决定」是伦理学问题，本 hub 只把效用当作既定输入，价值论本身见<a href=\"../ethics-foundations/ethical-theories/consequentialism\">后果主义</a>。而「人为何系统性地偏离理性」的认知机制，与<a href=\"../critical-thinking-argumentation/fallacies-biases/cognitive-biases\">认知偏误</a>相邻，本 hub 从规范落差的角度切入，那里从批判性思维的角度切入。</p>\n<p>前置知识很轻：会读简单的概率（期望、条件概率）与基本代数即可；公理证明部分需要一点集合与关系的耐心，但每一步都配了直觉解释。带着一个你正犹豫的真实决定来读，收获会最大。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"基础：决策论问什么、不问什么","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"why-decision-theory","title":"为何需要一套决策论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/foundations/why-decision-theory"},{"seq":2,"slug":"normative-vs-descriptive","title":"规范、描述与规定：三种问法之别","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/foundations/normative-vs-descriptive"},{"seq":3,"slug":"decision-model","title":"决策模型：状态、行动与结果","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/foundations/decision-model"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"utility","title":"效用：理性选择的技术核心","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/utility","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"expected-utility","title":"期望效用理论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/utility/expected-utility"},{"seq":2,"slug":"vnm-axioms","title":"冯·诺依曼–摩根斯坦公理","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/utility/vnm-axioms"},{"seq":3,"slug":"risk-attitudes","title":"风险态度与效用形状","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/utility/risk-attitudes"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"debates","title":"争论：标准框架开始撕裂的地方","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/debates","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"causal-vs-evidential","title":"因果决策论与证据决策论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/debates/causal-vs-evidential"},{"seq":2,"slug":"newcomb-problem","title":"Newcomb 问题","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/debates/newcomb-problem"},{"seq":3,"slug":"ambiguity-uncertainty","title":"模糊与奈特不确定性","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/debates/ambiguity-uncertainty"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"practice","title":"应用：理论撞上真实的人与真实的世界","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/practice","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"paradoxes","title":"悖论：Allais 与 Ellsberg","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/practice/paradoxes"},{"seq":2,"slug":"bounded-rationality","title":"有限理性","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/practice/bounded-rationality"},{"seq":3,"slug":"decision-theory-in-practice","title":"应用与边界","url":"/l-doc-books/h/philosophy-logic/decision-theory-philosophy/practice/decision-theory-in-practice"}]}]}